2026-09-27: explicit -fno-strict-aliasing admission, EvoIR 1.9.113.

Source SHA256 aa3ad4cd58d60356bbefb2d5e75839ebfb27e9a6a55cd9825badb729e0117902.
Executable SHA256 5e2d02991a6b0563828eefc0e0e9ae68c5dc33d1323ee0bf672d1c7108c9d6f6.
No release executable was overwritten.

The isolated program stores through differently typed, aliasing scalar pointers.
Both interpreters already returned zero without the flag, while the driver
rejected the actual flag and three application projectors omitted it (RED).
EvoCC has no C-type-derived disjointness or effective-type optimization. The
explicit disabling option now selects that existing behavior. It is preserved
by application and Kbuild command projection. This does not disable any object,
provenance, lifetime, alignment, initializedness or read-only access check.

GREEN: O0/O2 C-HIR/EvoIR execution, canonical IR and assembly are identical
with/without the option. A write through a cast to a const object still reports
E3014 in both interpreters. All 39 driver-option tests pass. Four fixed
GCC14/Clang19 O0/O2 controls compiled with -fno-strict-aliasing execute zero;
eight actual EvoCC O0/O2 / reference compiler O0/O2 native builds execute zero.
The positive -fstrict-aliasing option remains unsupported, not silently ignored.

Eight unchanged musl commands retain no-strict-aliasing, function/data sections
and standard excess precision. Outcomes/stdout/stderr are byte-identical when
only no-strict-aliasing is removed. Four units emit and assemble; the four
scalar-FP asm units retain E3021. Every remaining omission is still reported.
Read-only inspection of the full 1,339 recorded commands finds no remaining
omission of these four repaired option families. Remaining omissions are
assembler-only --noexecstack (forwarded to assembly), diagnostic policy,
GCC-specific tuning/alignment/frame options, -pipe and the replaced -o action.
Those remaining controls require their own documented accounting; this is
not a new full musl compile/libc-test result or permission to ignore unknown flags.

Changed-crate gate against 3343220: 530 PASS / 0 FAIL / 0 ignored, Clippy -D
warnings and fmt pass. The prior full-workspace checkpoint and section gate
retain their separate denominators. Logs: .build/floating-targeted/strict-20260927/
  alias-option-red.log, alias-projection-red.log, alias-option-green.log,
  no-alias-native.log, no-alias-musl-replay.log, alias-changed-gate.log.
